course: dictionary
lesson: 8263
title: Many meanings of ride
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings. The word «ride» is a good example. To work out which meaning is right, look at the words around it, because they are the context and they leave clues.
explain: «The speed a bike loses when it brakes turns into heat in the pads and rim, which is why they are hot after a long ride downhill.» Bikes are in the sentence, and a ride down a hill is a trip, so ride means a trip on a bike here.
explain: «A theme park posts its wait time, 45 minutes, so you can choose another ride.» A theme park is a place of fun machines, so ride here means a machine you can go on, like a roller coaster. Ask yourself: what word would fit in this place? Then put your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: «Ride» can be a verb (to ride, rides, rode, ridden, riding) or a noun (a ride, rides).
fact: To ride is to sit on something and travel on it, like a bike, horse or bus.
fact: To give someone a ride, which is a lift in the UK, is to take them in your car.
fact: «Everything rides on this game» means everything depends on this game.
exercise: «The speed a bike loses when it brakes turns into heat, which is why the brakes are hot after a long ride downhill.» What does ride mean here? | A kind of road sign | A machine at a fair | A horse that is wild | *A trip on a bike
exercise: «A theme park posts its wait time, so you can choose another ride.» What is a ride in this sentence? | A bus stop | A kind of ticket | *A machine at a theme park that you can go on | Something you cannot see
exercise: «Everything rides on this game.» What does rides on mean? | *It depends on it | It sits on top of it | It is painted on it | It travels across it
test: «You never ride up the inside of a lorry or truck at a junction, because the driver cannot see you.» What does this warn you not to do? | *Travel up the inside of a big lorry, where it is dangerous | Wave at the lorry driver | Check the lorry's tyres | Ride a horse past lorries
test: Your friend says, «Can you give me a ride to school?» What does a ride mean here? | A bike with a broken wheel | A machine at a fair | A trip on a horse | *A trip in your car
exam: Which sentence uses ride to mean that something depends on it? | *«Everything rides on this game.» | «A girl of eight rode in the front seat.» | «Ride the bus to school.» | «A pony ride costs five pounds.»
